summary:
  Once an address has five readings it is never read again.

history:
  A station's level moves with what it plays (one of the twenty had a range
  of 11.5 LU), so the oldest reading is replaced when the newest is thirty
  days old.

target:
  package/contents/ui/LoudLogic.js

find:
      return e[3].length < KEEP || nowS - e[1] > STALE_S;

replace:
      return e[3].length < KEEP;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_loudlogic.qml::test_five_readings_serve_until_the_newest_is_thirty_days_old.
  Line-neutral.
